WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:39.719
NO REGRETS:
“It was 

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:42.719
well worth doing prison time for The Pirate
Bay.”

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:47.700
This was the final battle cry of Pirate Bay
cofounder Fredrick Neij despite getting raided

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.700
by the police multiple times, being fined
46 million kroner, and being thrown in prison

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.739
alongside some of the most vile people on
Earth.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:01.090
In fact, Fredrick was the only person in his
entire prison that was there for a virtual

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.090
crime.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.770
Everyone else there was convicted of robbery,
assault, manslaughter, or worse.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.870
But, things were not too bad in prison says
Fredrick.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:14.260
He immersed himself with reading letters from
fans about how much the Pirate Bay meant to

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.260
them.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.900
This isn’t to say that Fredrick willing
turned himself in though.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:22.970
Like any normal human being, he very much
dreaded the idea of going to jail and he was

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:28.180
on the run for several years as one of the
most hated individuals by media organizations

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.240
around the world.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:34.460
But, eventually, the law did catch up with
him putting him behind bars.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:39.329
But, this only strengthened Fredrick’s personal
conviction as the letters reminded him of

00:01:39.329 --> 00:01:42.000
why did everything in the first place.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.079
Unlike other piracy website creators, Fredrick
wasn’t trying to make money or get rich

00:01:47.079 --> 00:01:48.680
or screw over big companies.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:52.030
He had founded The Pirate Bay out of principle.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:57.590
The idea that information, culture, and knowledge
should be shared freely around the world without

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:01.770
the interference of corporate greed, bureaucracy,
or political influence.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:06.740
In fact, Fredrick had been fighting for this
cause long before he co founded the Pirate

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.470
Bay or gained any sort of notoriety.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:13.980
Before his Pirate Bay days, Fredrick was part
of a Swedish anti copyright group that went

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:19.190
around the world engaging in piracy debates
and giving lectures about the right to information.

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:24.050
This is where Fredrick met the other founders
Gottfrid Svartholm and Peter Sunde.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:29.410
And together, they would go on to create one
of the most controversial yet legendary sites

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:30.860
of all time.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:36.190
So, here’s how the Pirate Bay went from
being an ideological effort to becoming an

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:41.750
international icon despite police raids, jail
time, and the efforts of the media industry

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.270
at large.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:53.110
THE SCALLYWAGS:
The story of the Pirate Bay dates back to

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:59.610
the late 1970s and early 1980s to the country
of Sweden where all three of our protagonists

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:00.780
were born.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:06.120
Not much is known about any of the founders’
childhoods, but from what we do know, it wasn’t

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.420
anything to brag about.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:13.530
Fredrick was the oldest of the bunch having
been born on April 27, 1978 in the city of

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.670
Jönköping Sweden.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:19.440
There’s rumors that he dropped out of high
school and it appears that he just stumbled

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.580
though his life one day at at time.

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.700
A similar story could be said about Gottfrid
as well who was the youngest of the bunch

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.489
having been born on October 17, 1984.

00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:34.180
Gottfrid was your classic computer nerd/hacker
of the 1990s and 2000s.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.580
Think Dennis Nedry from Jurassic Park.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.610
And then there was Peter Sunde who was the
only one that would be considered somewhat

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:46.230
successful by modern society, but this wasn’t
to say the his childhood was any better.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:50.709
Peter was born on September 13, 1978 in Uddevalla
Sweden.

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:53.790
At first, he life wasn’t all that bad.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:58.750
His mother was a staff consultant at a large
company and his father was a traveling mechanic.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:04.150
But, all of this fell apart when Peter’s
parents got a divorce when he was just 8 years

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.150
old.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:09.099
His mother would become clinically delusional
as she developed psychosis which resulted

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:12.439
in the family constantly moving all across
Scandanavia.

00:04:12.439 --> 00:04:17.739
Unsurprisingly, Peter would end up dropping
out of school in his teens, but there was

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:20.750
one saving grace: computers.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:25.620
Computers were Peter’s one and only escape
from his harsh realty and this led to him

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.800
becoming quite a skilled programmer.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:32.350
Ironically, if he had this same childhood
in modern times, it’s likely that he would’ve

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:37.560
become a lifeless social media addict like
myse..Anyways, things were different back

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:38.560
then.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.460
The people spending all of their time on computers
weren’t endlessly scrolling through TikTok.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.980
They were enthusiasts learning how to code
and hack systems, and this would catch the

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.770
attention of German technology company Siemens.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:55.460
Siemens is the people behind many of the IT
systems used at hospitals, and they would

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:59.850
hire Peter to upgrade their patient registration
system from being fingerprint based to being

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:00.930
retinal based.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:06.530
It seemed like a pretty good gig at first
glance, but Peter could not stand it at Siemens

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:07.560
after he joined.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.380
He would discover that his development efforts
were being used to identify and deport illegal

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:15.300
immigrants leading them to do unthinkable
things.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.780
You see, many of these immigrants would burn
their fingers on kitchen stoves before visiting

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:22.710
the hospital to avoid being identified.

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:27.750
This was actually one of the main reasons
that Siemens wanted to switch to a retinal

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:28.750
system.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.740
But this simply gave Peter nightmares about
immigrants poking out their eyes like Victor

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:33.740
Creel.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:37.840
He tried to take it up with his managers,
but this simply gave him the title of being

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:40.540
negative and difficult to work with.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:44.690
Being drained from work everyday, the only
solace Peter found was during the evenings

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:50.370
when he scrolled through online forums leading
him to discover the world of piracy.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:58.380
FOUNDING THE PIRATE BAY:
Peter’s piracy journey started with him

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:04.000
swapping music and movies on invite only servers
which led him to meeting fellow scallywag:

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.210
Fredrick Neij.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:10.110
Fredrick introduced Peter to the file-sharing
movement and to the newly founded anti copyright

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:13.190
organization: Piratbyrån or The Pirate Bureau.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:19.069
Piratbyrån was founded on August 1, 2003
by a bunch of societal outcasts just like

00:06:19.069 --> 00:06:21.699
Peter, Fredrick, and Gottfrid.

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:26.060
Their goal was to make information available
to people of all backgrounds and stature,

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:29.300
and promote free speech above everythign else.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:34.180
Not saying I agree with how they went about
doing this, but honestly, it does seem like

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:38.301
their intentions were way more pure than most
of the people who actually control the world

00:06:38.301 --> 00:06:39.301
today.

00:06:39.301 --> 00:06:42.380
With this idea in mind, the group got to work.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:45.759
Some members tried opposing pro copyright
lobbyist groups.

00:06:45.759 --> 00:06:49.470
Others traveled the world and gave lectures
on radio and TV.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.100
Our trio decided to create a website.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.610
This was specifically Fredrick’s idea.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:59.220
He wanted to create a Bittorrent tracker and
he would recruit the help of Peter and Gottfrid

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.590
for the IT and coding side of things.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:05.940
Given the relative simplicity of the website,
Peter and Gottfrid had this up and running

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:11.530
in no time and Piratbyrån would launch the
website on September 15, 2003.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:16.100
This was actually just one of many websites
that this trio launched.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:21.020
Moving into 2004, Fredrick and Gottfrid would
create a full on internet service provider

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:23.800
and web hosting company called PRQ.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:27.100
Don’t be fooled though, this was no AT&amp;T.

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:33.150
With PRQ, Fredrick and Gottfrid looked to
give an online voice to anyone and everyone

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:36.310
regardless of what they stood for or did.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:43.520
This included some unheard and repressed voices
but it also included a bunch of creeps literally.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:49.280
There were a bunch of forums hosted on PRQ
that advocated for how should I say it: unorthodox

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:50.280
relationships.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.090
Though Fredrick and Gottfrid definitely did
not agree with everything that was hosted

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:59.300
on their platform, they defended all of their
customers equally citing freedom speech.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:03.880
Something else that sparked a bunch of controversy
was yet another one this duo’s ventures:

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.990
Americas Dumbest Soldiers.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:08.770
Honestly, this one was quite distasteful.

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:13.550
The website consisted of a list of deceased
American soldiers and it prompted people to

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.020
vote on how dumb their deaths were.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:19.439
Little to say, this site didn’t stay up
for very long.

00:08:19.439 --> 00:08:23.750
While these other ventures definitely caused
a scene by themselves, it turned out that

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:27.280
the trio’s original venture would have the
greatest sticking power.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:30.699
And luckily for them, it was pretty cheap
to run.

00:08:30.699 --> 00:08:35.209
Afterall, the Pirate Bay didn’t actually
have any file hosting or server to client

00:08:35.209 --> 00:08:37.200
downloading abilites built in.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.630
The site simply connected people with a library
of links and all of the downloading took place

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.190
using peer to peer protocols.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:47.339
So, the trio just had to ensure that they
had enough server capacity to handle all of

00:08:47.339 --> 00:08:50.360
the search volume, indexing, sorting, and
filtering itself.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:56.000
But, to their surprise it didn’t take long
for this itself to become unmanageable.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:05.140
THE LEGENDARY RISE:
As the Pirate Bay exploded it popularity,

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:10.230
it became abundantly clear that this could
no longer be treated as a side project.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:16.899
So, in October of 2004, the trio would transition
the site into being a standalone non profit

00:09:16.899 --> 00:09:19.450
based in the Seychelles, though this is disputed.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:23.720
If you also have no idea what this place,
you’re not alone.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:28.680
The Seychelles is an East African country
that’s composed of a 115 islands and it

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:32.120
just so happened to be the perfect place to
setup a shell company.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.940
Now, they had an entity.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.340
All they needed was infrastructure.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:37.970
Enter Carl Lundström.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.170
This guy was one of five heirs to the Wasabrod
fortune.

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:45.650
I’ve actually never heard of this company,
but they’re super big.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:50.399
They’re extremely popular across Scandinavia
and they’re actually the largest crisp bread

00:09:50.399 --> 00:09:51.580
producer in the world.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:56.520
By the time Carl turned 22, this company would
be sold to a Swiss pharmaceutical company

00:09:56.520 --> 00:10:02.180
called Sandoz which made Carl a mega millionaire
by the time most of us would even graduate

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:03.180
college.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:08.089
Carl would turnaround and use this wealth
to fund a variety of extreme political movements

00:10:08.089 --> 00:10:12.019
and it wasn’t long till he crossed paths
with our protagonists.

00:10:12.019 --> 00:10:16.190
He would agree to provide the Pirate Bay with
all of the required servers and infrastructure

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:21.090
and before you knew it, the Pirate Bay would
become a fully funded venture making copyright

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.820
holders around the world cry.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:25.899
But, they weren’t crying for long.

00:10:25.899 --> 00:10:28.890
They were hurt and they were hurt bad.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:35.010
Hollywood claims that in 2006 alone, piracy
cost them $6.1 billion.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:40.140
And the biggest culprit enabling this asinine
behavior was the Swedish site that was just

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:43.269
one Google search away: the Pirate Bay.

00:10:43.269 --> 00:10:46.709
Naturally, Hollywood wanted revenge, they
wanted justice.

00:10:46.709 --> 00:10:51.430
So, they marched over to the Swedish authorities
and demanded that the Pirate Bay be taken

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.970
down as soon as possible.

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:56.560
This was met with a chuckle from Sweden.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.060
I’m not even kidding.

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:01.730
You see, Sweden is surprisingly chill about
copyright and patents.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:06.790
In fact, they have a full on political party
called the Pirate Party who’s entire focus

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:09.200
is to reform copyright law.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:13.930
Hollywood was gobsmacked and they would take
their grievances to the good old USA.

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:18.550
Surely, their hundreds of millions of lobbying
dollars would actually earn them some respect

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:21.200
from the American authorities and they were
right.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:26.089
The US would turn around and go “Yo Sweden,
you better shutdown those mischievous rascals

00:11:26.089 --> 00:11:27.089
you got there.

00:11:27.089 --> 00:11:30.670
You don’t want us to bring out the stick
and impose trade sanctions through the World

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:32.779
Trade Organizations right?”

00:11:32.779 --> 00:11:37.589
And to that Sweden would respond “Your wish
is our command” and they would go ahead

00:11:37.589 --> 00:11:42.000
and raid the Pirate Bay’s servers in Stockholm
on May 31, 2006.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:46.180
There was so much equipment that the Swedish
police would end up filling three trucks worth

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.329
of computer equipment and servers.

00:11:48.329 --> 00:11:52.760
Surely, this would put an end to the nonsense
they thought.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:59.260
Ummm, the Pirate Bay would be back up in just
3 days.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:07.520
HOLLYWOOD STRIKES BACK:
You’re probably wondering, how was the trio

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:10.110
able to restart the Pirate Bay so quickly?

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:13.950
Well, the answer is that the Pirate Bay is
nothing.

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:17.250
It’s really just a massive excel sheet with
a bunch of links.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:22.200
In fact, the entirety of the Pirate Bay can
be compressed into a 90 megabyte zip file.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:27.300
So, they didn’t have to maintain massive
convoluted code bases and repositories or

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.180
enterprise resource planning software.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:34.560
All of the servers and equipment were simply
there to support the extraordinary traffic.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:38.579
So, as soon as they were able to find new
infrastructure, they were able to upload their

00:12:38.579 --> 00:12:42.530
tiny little zip file and go live in no time.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:46.610
This time, they chose to put their servers
in a more discrete location somewhere in the

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:51.540
Netherlands so that the police couldn’t
just turn around and raid them again.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.130
Hollywood was triggered.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:57.930
Not only was the Pirate Bay back up and running,
but the police raid had simply drawn even

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.820
more attention to the website.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:05.110
Clearly, Hollywood didn’t have much power
in Sweden, so they turned their focus to American

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.110
companies.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:10.779
They might not be able to shutdown the Pirate
Bay, but maybe they could prevent you from

00:13:10.779 --> 00:13:11.779
accessing it.

00:13:11.779 --> 00:13:16.510
They started working with Google, Facebook,
Microsoft, and ISPs to suppress the sharing

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:20.540
and searching of Pirate Bay links, but this
only made things worse.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:25.440
Here’s the thing, when you tell people not
to do something, that’s when they want to

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:28.620
do it even more and this couldn’t be any
truer with the Pirate Bay.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.230
Just because Facebook or Google suppressed
Pirate Bay links doesn’t mean jack.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:37.290
You don’t have to be a rocket scientist
to go directly to the Pirate Bay and search

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:40.690
up whatever you want, and that was exactly
what was happening.

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:47.550
By 2008, the Pirate Bay became the 97th most
visited website on the entire internet, and

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:52.240
they were even having talks about selling
the website to Global Gaming Factory X AB

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:54.710
for $8.5 million.

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:59.740
It was becoming abundantly clear that there
was only one way to stop this madness: strike

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:00.910
the tent.

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:07.449
On January 31, 2008, Swedish prosecutors would
file charges against Gottfrid, Fredrick, Peter,

00:14:07.449 --> 00:14:08.490
and Carl.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:11.350
From the very beginning, this was an open
and shut case.

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:15.650
The Pirate Bay’s lawyers tried to defend
that the Pirate Bay was simply hosting links,

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:20.090
and that it wasn’t actually encouraging
or enabling piracy.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:23.970
If you want, you could use the site to share
opensource software.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:30.020
While this was technically true, I mean, let’s
face it, these guys were literally part of

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:33.860
Piratbyrån and all of this was completely
intentional.

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:39.820
So, their argument was quickly shut down and
on April 17, 2009, all four of them would

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:45.470
be sentenced to one year in jail along with
a 30 million kroner fine which is about $3.5

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:46.519
million.

00:14:46.519 --> 00:14:50.970
They would try appealing and this did result
in shorter prison sentences.

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:55.070
Fredrick would be down to 10 months, Peter
would be down to 8 months, and Carl would

00:14:55.070 --> 00:14:56.620
be down to 4 months.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:03.089
But, the appeal also came with a larger fine
of 46 million Kroner or $6.5 million.

00:15:03.089 --> 00:15:08.019
The walls were closing in, and there was only
one thing that the trio could do: get on the

00:15:08.019 --> 00:15:10.160
run.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:20.139
UNSTOPPABLE LEGACY:
If you’re wanted by Hollywood at large for

00:15:20.139 --> 00:15:24.529
causing billions of dollars worth of lost
revenue, you would think that it would be

00:15:24.529 --> 00:15:25.950
a good to lay low.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:31.040
But all three of our protagonists would do
the exact opposite.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:36.000
Fredrick would run away to Laos/Thailand and
he would create yet another file sharing site

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.240
called BayFiles in 2011.

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:43.839
Apparently, this website was supposed to comply
with copyright rules, but you can take that

00:15:43.839 --> 00:15:45.459
for what you will.

00:15:45.459 --> 00:15:50.110
Not only did Fredrick launch another site,
but he would regularly cross the border between

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:54.149
Laos and Thailand because he had residences
in both countries.

00:15:54.149 --> 00:15:59.170
In fact, he crossed the border almost 30 times
before getting caught in November of 2014

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:05.050
at which point he would be deported back to
Sweden where he spent 200 days in jail.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:09.380
Atleast Fredrick created another side that
was legal atleast on the front.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:14.500
Gottfrid on the other hand would run away
to Cambodia and go full on spy mode and became

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:17.149
a regular hacker for Wikileaks.

00:16:17.149 --> 00:16:22.140
He would literally infiltrate Denmark’s
social security and driver’s license databases.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:26.240
I don’t think that you’d be surprised
to hear that when he was caught in August

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:31.949
of 2012, his prison sentence would be upped
to three and a half years, but he would be

00:16:31.949 --> 00:16:33.890
let go after 3 years.

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:39.430
And finally as for Peter, well, my man straight
up joined Finland’s Pirate party and ran

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:42.170
for European Parliament in the 2014 election.

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:46.810
Let’s just say, he was arrested a few days
after the election and had to serve five months

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:47.889
in jail.

00:16:47.889 --> 00:16:52.860
By late 2014, all three founders were not
only disconnected from the Pirate Bay, but

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.370
they were all straight up in jail.

00:16:55.370 --> 00:17:01.130
So, prosecuters figured that this was the
perfect time to end this once and for all.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:06.840
On December 9, 2014, the police would conduct
yet another raid on the Pirate Bay and they

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:09.350
would shut down the original website once
and for all.

00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:14.120
Surely, the founders couldn’t pull any quick
ones this time right?

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.020
Well, they were right.

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:21.030
None of the founders would try to restart
the Pirate Bay after their jail sentence.

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:23.890
Fredrick would return Laos and get a job in
IT.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:28.470
Peter would work on a micropayments system
called Flattr and a messaging platform called

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:29.470
Hemlis.

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:33.760
Gottfrid would also return to the IT sector
and move on from the Pirate Bay, but none

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.760
of this mattered.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:38.890
Yes, the founders were done and out, but there
were thousands of people wanting to carry

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:40.460
on the legacy.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:44.799
Remember how we talked about it being really
easy to store the entirety of the Pirate Bay.

00:17:44.799 --> 00:17:50.299
Well, it turns out that a lot of people had
been regularly saving copies of the website.

00:17:50.299 --> 00:17:55.460
So whenever one version of the website is
taken down, it’s just a matter of time until

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:58.840
another one pops up with a slightly different
domain.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:04.200
At first, prosecutors tried taking down these
websites one after another, but it quickly

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:09.950
became evident that this was simply a waste
of time, effort, and resources because the

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:13.980
legacy of the Pirate Bay was truly unstoppable.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:25.390
THE FINAL SAY:
In the end, the Pirate Bay started off as

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:31.320
a project created by a bunch of misfits and
outcasts, but it quickly turned into the icon

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:35.740
of the internet and the worst nightmare of
copyright holders.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:41.660
Hollywood tried burying it, shredding it,
and burning it, but in the end they decided

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:45.700
to just give it all away because what other
choice did they really have.

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:50.409
Also, if you’re wondering about what happened
to the fine well here’s what Peter had to

00:18:50.409 --> 00:18:51.610
say about it.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:55.210
During the press conference following the
verdict, Peter would hold up a sign saying

00:18:55.210 --> 00:19:01.380
that he owes the government 31 million kroner
and that that confession is all that the government

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:02.380
would get.

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:06.360
If that wasn’t clear enough, he would go
onto clarify that he doesn’t have the money

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:11.320
he didn’t have any money and even if he
did, he’d rather burn everything and not

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:13.419
even give them the ashes.

00:19:13.419 --> 00:19:17.710
And that right there is the legendary history
of the Pirate Bay.

